Subject: ci(loops-routing): fetch full history, matching the test job

The loops-routing job's checkout is shallow (no fetch-depth), while the
test job pins fetch-depth: 0 with an explicit rationale. The gap was
latent until claude/plugins-pin-stability grew two review-loop
calibration documents: check-workflow-state's plugins-pin reconciliation
then had to resolve the recorded pin commit via `git show`, which a
shallow clone cannot serve (the pin commit is not fetched), so
tests/task-plan-binding-durability.tests.sh's P3 cases fail in CI while
passing in every full-depth checkout. Observed on PR #354 run
32910347404 (macos + ubuntu red, windows green because the sh suite does
not run there).

Apply from the repository root:

    git apply --check docs/ci-staging/loops-routing-fetch-depth.patch
    git apply docs/ci-staging/loops-routing-fetch-depth.patch

---
--- a/.github/workflows/test.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/test.yml
@@ -340,6 +340,14 @@ jobs:
     timeout-minutes: 20
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1
+        with:
+          # Full history, matching the test job: check-workflow-state's
+          # plugins-pin reconciliation resolves recorded pin commits via git
+          # show, which a shallow clone cannot serve (the pin commit is not
+          # fetched). task-plan-binding-durability's P3 fixtures depend on it
+          # whenever a live plugins reference has grown past the committed
+          # contracts' pins.
+          fetch-depth: 0

       - name: Test template-validator parity (bash)
         shell: bash
